program RopeTool
arg -h
status 0
output
ropetool [options] command arguments...

  -h, --help
      Display help message and exit.

cat A B  Print the concatenation of A and B.


sub S START LEN  Print the substring of S from START, LEN characters.


len S  Print the length of S.


fetch S I  Print the character of S at index I.


cmp A B  Print -1, 0 or 1: how A compares to B.


find S PATTERN FROM  Print the index of PATTERN in S at or after FROM, or -1.


repeat S N  Print N concatenated copies of S.


insert S POS INS  Print S with INS inserted before index POS.


remove S POS LEN  Print S with LEN characters removed starting at POS.


rfind S PATTERN BEFORE  Print the index of the last PATTERN in S at or before BEFORE, or -1.


split S SEP  Print each piece of S split on SEP, one per line.


trim S  Print S with leading and trailing whitespace removed.


triml S  Print S with leading whitespace removed.


trimr S  Print S with trailing whitespace removed.


upper S  Print S with ASCII letters uppercased.


lower S  Print S with ASCII letters lowercased.


capitalize S  Print S with its first character uppercased (ASCII only).


uncapitalize S  Print S with its first character lowercased (ASCII only).


escaped S  Print S with special and non-printable characters escaped.


make LEN CH  Print a rope of LEN copies of CH.


bigcat N1 CH1 N2 CH2  Print the length of N1 copies of CH1 concatenated with N2 copies of CH2.


indexchar S CH FROM  Print the index of CH in S at or after FROM, or -1.


rindexchar S CH BEFORE  Print the index of CH in S at or before BEFORE, or -1.


contains S CH FROM  Print TRUE or FALSE: whether CH occurs in S at or after FROM.


overwrite S POS NEW  Print S with the characters from POS replaced by NEW.


head S COUNT PAD  Print the first COUNT characters of S, padded with PAD if COUNT exceeds Length(S).


tail S COUNT PAD  Print the last COUNT characters of S, padded with PAD if COUNT exceeds Length(S).


containspattern S PATTERN FROM  Print TRUE or FALSE: whether PATTERN occurs in S at or after FROM.


iterate S  Print each character of S, one per line, via Ropes.Iterate.


iterator S  Print each character of S, one per line, via Ropes.NewIterator/Get/Incr.


lines FILE  Read FILE (standard input if FILE is -) and print each line's length, a space, and the line.


readfile FILE  Read all of FILE, byte for byte, and print its length, a space, and its contents escaped.


blit S SRCSTART DST DSTSTART LEN  Print DST with LEN characters of S from SRCSTART copied into it at DSTSTART.


replace S POS LEN BY  Print S with the LEN characters at POS replaced by BY.


replacechar S POS CH  Print S with the character at POS replaced by CH.


count S PATTERN  Print the number of non-overlapping occurrences of PATTERN in S.


countset S CHARS  Print the number of characters of S that are any of CHARS.


indexset S CHARS FROM  Print the index of the first character of S at or after FROM that is any of CHARS, or -1.


rindexset S CHARS BEFORE  Print the index of the last character of S at or before BEFORE that is any of CHARS, or -1.


nonblank S FROM  Print the index of the first non-space character of S at or after FROM, or -1.


rnonblank S BEFORE  Print the index of the last non-space character of S at or before BEFORE, or -1.


findtoken S CHARS FROM  Print START LEN: the first run of characters of S at or after FROM that are any of CHARS.


translate S FROM TO  Print S with each character in FROM replaced by the one at the same place in TO.


cmpnocase A B  Print -1, 0 or 1: how A compares to B, ignoring ASCII case.


hash S  Print the hash of S.


hashnocase S  Print the hash of S, ignoring ASCII case.


findnocase S PATTERN FROM  Print the index of PATTERN in S at or after FROM, ignoring ASCII case, or -1.


countnocase S PATTERN  Print the number of non-overlapping occurrences of PATTERN in S, ignoring ASCII case.

